Z||000002||frontal lobe||04-04-2001||02:00 PM||||No, sorry, can't relate with you on that one.  But since we have established that we are going to give out WAY more information on this thread than anyone wants, here I go:<P>I've only vomited twice in my entire life because I hate to do it so bad.  Once was when I was 6 or 7 when at school a neighborhood kid with cerebral palsy lost control and accidently slammed my head into the concrete block gym wall.  I was then able to hold everything down for the next 37 years until I had my acl repaired, and during the ride home in the back of the minivan that afternoon the anesthesia and motion got me and I had vomitus #2.<P>So I'm pulling into the driveway last night about 6pm and see my 5 y.o. daughter about a block away walking down the street by herself with the dog, looking distressed.  She says she was walking the dog with another of my daughters when my 8 y.o. daughter vomited all her supper all over the curb, and she's still there (about 2 blocks away) and wants someone to go get her.  So I'm thinking food poisoning, or appendicitis, or something.  So we get in the car and drive the 2 blocks and I get there and she's looking fine standing by the roadside next to you-know-what (beef stew for supper that night, too, as I found out later).  I asked her what happened.  She said the dog had pooped and she had a bag along to clean it up but got a big whiff and...<P>So I get up this morning and my wife tells me my 5 y.o. just vomited her breakfast.  What???  Is there food poisoning going around, or some virus?  No, my oldest daughter has been having a lot of phlegm from allergies and at breakfast accidentally coughed up a huge loogy (spelling?) and my 5 year old was so grossed out by it...<P>Ahhh, who needs money?  It's the memories we make in life that we will cherish the most.||||reg||1
